00:27:57.780 --> 00:28:00.500
I wanted to ask, what's the
coolest or your favorite?

00:28:00.500 --> 00:28:02.460
What's the most
interesting API you've

00:28:02.460 --> 00:28:06.180
come across in all your
time working with APIs?

00:28:06.180 --> 00:28:08.830
ALAN HO: Oh.

00:28:08.830 --> 00:28:10.390
What's the coolest API?

00:28:14.890 --> 00:28:18.680
I would say, very
recently, the Uber APIs

00:28:18.680 --> 00:28:21.530
are the most interesting.

00:28:21.530 --> 00:28:28.160
The Uber API--
Uber provides APIs

00:28:28.160 --> 00:28:32.570
so that you can call
a cab from anywhere.

00:28:32.570 --> 00:28:36.760
And this allows you to-- they
actually do multiple things.

00:28:36.760 --> 00:28:38.690
They allow you to call.

00:28:38.690 --> 00:28:42.110
They have an API to pick
up anybody or anything

00:28:42.110 --> 00:28:44.300
and deliver it to
somewhere else.

00:28:44.300 --> 00:28:47.180
And that drastically
changes how local commerce

00:28:47.180 --> 00:28:49.827
is done because when
you create a store

00:28:49.827 --> 00:28:52.160
and things of that sort,
there's an automatic assumption

00:28:52.160 --> 00:28:55.970
of how-- you create
stores based on how far it

00:28:55.970 --> 00:28:58.635
takes to drive there or
the reach of the store.

00:28:58.635 --> 00:29:00.260
And suddenly, when
you have an API that

00:29:00.260 --> 00:29:02.780
lets you deliver almost
anything to anywhere

00:29:02.780 --> 00:29:06.470
within a city in
less than 30 minutes,

00:29:06.470 --> 00:29:13.910
you drastically change how
stores should be thought about

00:29:13.910 --> 00:29:16.720
and how you can
connect with customers.

00:29:16.720 --> 00:29:18.260
And they also have
a cool API, too,

00:29:18.260 --> 00:29:21.800
that even if you're in an
Uber and going to the store,

00:29:21.800 --> 00:29:25.880
you can monitor what every
single person is doing.

00:29:25.880 --> 00:29:30.320
And then, assuming the user
gives permission, and even

00:29:30.320 --> 00:29:34.370
let them know about products
that you're about to see

00:29:34.370 --> 00:29:37.670
or before you get
into the store itself.

00:29:37.670 --> 00:29:42.320
So they've created this
end-to-end trip experience,

00:29:42.320 --> 00:29:45.680
which is really going to
change how people build apps

00:29:45.680 --> 00:29:48.650
as well as how people
actually-- potentially

00:29:48.650 --> 00:29:55.070
how cities can be arranged for
shopping as well as living.

00:29:55.070 --> 00:29:58.940
So I think that is probably
the most game-changing API

00:29:58.940 --> 00:30:00.462
that I've worked with so far.

00:30:00.462 --> 00:30:01.670
FRANCESC CAMPOY FLORES: Cool.

